  dict(title="Create the brand channel (the 'publish' destination)",
       body="In Telegram create a new channel 'Kopi Kaki Feed (Training)', add your bot as an administrator with permission to post. Then list targets to find its ID.",
       cmd="hermes send --list telegram",
       expect="Your channel appears as telegram:<channel_id>. Copy it."),
  dict(title="Make risky commands ask first",
       body="Create this lab's output folder and approval log, and switch approvals to manual so every dangerous terminal command pauses for you. Be clear about what this does and does not cover: approval modes gate risky TERMINAL commands; the publishing gate in this lab is a rule the agent follows (prompt-enforced, written into AGENTS.md). Lab 4 shows a runtime-enforced gate (a blocked task only you can release).",
       cmd="cp -Rn data/* ~/kopi-kaki/\nmkdir -p ~/kopi-kaki/outputs/lab03\ncp ~/kopi-kaki/templates/approval-log.csv ~/kopi-kaki/outputs/lab03/approval-log.csv\nhermes config set approvals.mode manual"),
  dict(title="Run one approval cycle by hand",
       where="Telegram → your bot",
       prompt="Approval workflow for #ShiokColdBrew (standing rule - add it to ~/kopi-kaki/AGENTS.md too):\n1. Take the next post with status \"draft\" from ~/kopi-kaki/outputs/lab02/content-calendar-v2.csv, set its status to \"pending-approval\" and send it to me here with its post id, image, platform and date. End with: Reply APPROVE <post_id>, EDIT <post_id>: <changes> or REJECT <post_id>.\n2. Whenever I reply APPROVE <post_id>, read that row from the CSV - it must say \"pending-approval\" - then post the caption and image to telegram:<channel_id>, set the status to \"published\" and append a row to ~/kopi-kaki/outputs/lab03/approval-log.csv.\n3. EDIT: apply my changes, re-check with kopi-brand-voice, keep \"pending-approval\" and send it again. REJECT: set \"rejected\" and log it.\n4. Never publish a row that is not \"pending-approval\" and never without my APPROVE.",
       expect="You receive the draft with its post id; after APPROVE <post_id> it appears in the channel, the CSV says published and approval-log.csv has a row."),
